6.NTH FIBONNACI LAST DIGIT 
Given a number n, find the last digit of the nth Fibonacci number. 
The Fibonacci sequence is a series in which each number is the sum of the previous two numbers, 
where F(0) = 0, F(1) = 1, and F(n) = F(n-1) + F(n-2) for n >= 2.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static int fib(int n) {
                int a=0,b=1,c=0;
                if(n==0){
                    return 0;
                }
                if(n==1){
                    return 1;
                }
                for(int i=2;i<=n;i++){
                    c=(a+b)%10;
                    a=b;
                    b=c;
                }
                return c;
            }
        }
