8.PERFECT NUMBER : 
Given a number n, check if the number is perfect or not. 
A number is said to be perfect if sum of all its factors excluding the number itself is equal to the number.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static boolean isPerfect(int n) {
                if(n<=1){
                    return false;
                }
                int sum=1;
                for(int i=2;i*i<=n;i++){
                    if(n%i==0){
                        sum+=i;
                        if(i!=n/i){
                            sum+=n/i;
                        }
                    }
                }
                return sum==n;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/perfect-numbers3207/1


